{"id": "bZGBTCE02RM", "title": "The True Healer", "description": "We live in a time where healing feels almost entirely mechanical. You feel pain, you see a doctor, you receive treatment, and if things improve the credit usually goes to the medicine or the procedure.\n\nIslam doesn’t reject any of those means. In fact, it encourages us to seek them. But it quietly corrects the way the heart understands them. A doctor can diagnose, prescribe, and treat, but the ability for a body to recover was never in their hands to begin with.\n\nEvery recovery, every closing wound, every fever that breaks, and every illness that lifts happens only because Allah allows the body to heal.\n\nThat’s why the Prophet ﷺ taught us to ask Allah as Ash-Shaafy, the One who heals completely. Not the One who merely reduces pain for a moment, but the One who can restore entirely and remove harm in ways no medicine can guarantee.\n\nSo the believer takes the means seriously, but the heart never attaches itself to the means. The prescription may be in the doctor’s hand, but healing itself remains with Allah.\n\nWatch Episode 23 of ''The Name I Need'' with Dr. Omar Suleiman: yqn.io/ct5x", "channel": "Yaqeen Institute", "kind": "lectures", "single_speaker_hint": null, "playlists": [], "seconds": 81, "is_short": true}
